The chord 10 : 12 : 14 : 17 which I have tried on Appunn's tonometer in its inversions, is a comparatively smooth discord superior to the tempered form. But the chord is really due to tempered intonation only. For further notes on this chord see App. XX. sect. E. art. @@A0@@
